osed","locked":true,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2017-03-03T16:29:43Z","updated_at":"2023-06-14T00:01:44Z","closed_at":"2023-04-28T05:52:07Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\r\n- Gitea version (or commit ref): 1.0.0+373-gd76d67d\r\n- Database (use `[x]`):\r\n  - [ ] PostgreSQL\r\n  - [x] MySQL\r\n  - [ ] SQLite\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nThe repository order feature works fine but I find it a little bit confusing. By default, the order is made on \"Most recent\" which means \"Most recently **created**\". But in the repository listing, there is only the last modification date which doesn't match the order.\r\nA tiny improvement would be to add a label like so:\r\n\r\n```\r\nCreated: 2 month ago - Updated : 2 days ago\r\n```\r\nI think I would be more understandable. \r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\n<img width=\"553\" alt=\"explorer_-_w_git_hosting\" src=\"https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/1597611/23559287/c6fb24e0-0036-11e7-92a3-8dac13fcf209.png\">\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"lunny","id":81045,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81045?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny","html_url":"https://github.com/lunny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lunny/events{/pri